<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.8.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01875</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.8.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>fe897db4-ab9e-4cc1-8d79-394c99b947a8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="13e5d43f-0171-4ebf-bf68-39abef4954ec" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Choose the expression that best describes the diagram.
          
          <figure><media alt=""><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a4c39cadbd12167dc25e8a8977547823585c8403"/></media></figure></para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+5x+8\).</para><para>\((2x +5)(x +3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+14x + 23\).</para><para>\((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\).</para><para>\((2x +5)(x +3)\) is equivalent to \(30x^2\). </para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\).</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4. </para><para>The correct answer is \((2x+5)(x+3)\) is equivalent to \(2x^2+11x+15\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="279bb73a-6893-4a2d-b527-807bee0fa839" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>In questions a–d, match each expanded quadratic expression with an equivalent expression written as a product.</para>
      <para>\(x^2+12x+32\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((x+2)(x+6)\) </para><para>\((x+4)(x+2)\)</para><para>\((x+8)(x+4)\)</para><para>\((x+2)(x+3)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((x+8)(x+4)\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.3.</para><para>The correct answer is: \((x+8)(x+4)\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="8e7633c5-78da-49c3-b6a7-e6265f139b84" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> \(x^2+5x+6\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((x+2)(x+6)\)</para><para>\((x+4)(x+2)\)</para><para>\((x+8)(x+4)\)</para><para>\((x+2)(x+3)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((x+2)(x+3)\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para><para>The correct answer is: \((x+2)(x+3)\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="5d9dd332-aeb9-4237-affe-cd381e9dd585" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(x^2+6x+8\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((x+2)(x+6)\)</para><para>\((x+4)(x+2)\)</para><para>\((x+8)(x+4)\)</para><para>\((x+2)(x+3)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((x+4)(x+2)\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para><para>The correct answer is:\((x+4)(x+2)\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="224fe3bf-30c3-4dc2-a62b-aaa67c1a3c84" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>\(x^2+8x+12\)</para>
      <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\((x+2)(x+6)\)</para><para>\((x+4)(x+2)\)</para><para>\((x+8)(x+4)\)</para><para>\((x+2)(x+3)\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \((x+2)(x+6)\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.3.</para><para>The correct answer is:\((x+2)(x+6)\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="a598cde7-4fc5-490f-833a-0b5c704e9fcf" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para><emphasis>Select three </emphasis>expressions that are equivalent to \(x^2+4x\).</para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(x(x+4)\), \((x+2)^2-4\), \((x+4)x\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.8.2-7.8.4. </para><para>The correct answers are: \(x(x+4)\), \((x+2)^2-4\), \((x+4)x\).
      </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="5fc3f3a4-158c-4131-977c-33bba99944f5" class="multiple-choice"><problem><newline/><para>Tyler drew a diagram to expand \((x+5)(2x+3)\).</para>
      <para> Tyler’s diagram is incorrect. Choose the sentence that describes Tyler’s mistake.</para>
        <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>Tyler added 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of multiplying them.</para><para>Tyler multiplied 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of adding them.</para><para>Tyler should have labeled the top \(2x\) and 5 and the side \(x\) and 3.</para><para>Tyler should have labeled the top \(x\) and 3 and the side \(2x\) and 5.</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! Tyler added 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of multiplying them. </para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.
      </para><para>The correct answer is: Tyler added 5 and 2 and 5 and 3 instead of multiplying them. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="740ac6b4-bf17-4ecd-ae4e-ae1e88a74c1f" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> What is the correct expanded form of \((x+5)(2x+3)\)?</para>
        <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(3x+8\)</para><para>\(30x^2\)</para><para>\(2x^2+10x+8\)</para><para>\(2x^2+13x+15\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(2x^2+13x+15\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.8.4.</para><para>The correct answer is : \(2x^2+13x+15\).
      </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
